{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794931463,"nonce":"PoaHAdimKqyKc6ruG5WKAxCc1fk=","message":"While validating c878f2a's hxn-av AAC decoder on unthreaded Emscripten, hxn package generated a wasm link.xml containing macOS AudioToolbox/VideoToolbox frameworks. xavi-backend is both a build dependency and a target dependency: Cargo reports build-script-executed messages for the host and wasm copies. Linked::read currently merges all of them. The wasm native-static-libs file is empty and correctly contains no Apple frameworks, but host build-dependency messages contaminate its linker XML.\n\nScope cross-target build-script metadata to out_dir beneath the selected target directory. Add a fixture with both host and target build-script messages, preserving target search paths and libraries while excluding host-only frameworks. Rebuild hxn-av packages on both emcc modes and keep ordinary native/mobile linkage covered. This is a tooling defect, not a browser codec dependency on Apple frameworks.","files":null}]}